{"name":"Chablis","hex":"#fde9e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Chablis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in Yonne department, Bourgogne-Franche-Comté, France.","The winegrowing region around the town."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A variety of dry white wine from this region"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Chablis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chablis","blocks":[{"text":"Chablis is a town and commune in the Yonne department in Bourgogne-Franche-Comté in north-central France."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Chablis_and_Premier_Cru_Vaulorent.jpg/330px-Chablis_and_Premier_Cru_Vaulorent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chablis"},{"title":"Chablis (AOC)","blocks":[{"text":"Chablis is the northernmost Appellation d'origine contrôlée of the Burgundy region in France. Its cool climate produces wines with more acidity and less fruitiness than warmer regions growing Chardonnay vines. These often have a \"flinty\" note, sometimes described as \"goût de pierre à fusil\", and sometimes as \"steely\". The Chablis AOC is required to use Chardonnay grapes solely."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Chablis_and_Premier_Cru_Vaulorent.jpg/330px-Chablis_and_Premier_Cru_Vaulorent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chablis_(AOC)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Chablis_Hotel_de_ville.jpg/500px-Chablis_Hotel_de_ville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Chablis_Hotel_de_ville.jpg/1280px-Chablis_Hotel_de_ville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Chablis_H